          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            This entry relates to a series of papers, beginning with
            %a{:href => "#PHCTIntro"} Barwick-Dotto-Glasman-Nardin-Shah 16
            which aim to provide common foundations for several different parts of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parametrized+homotopy+theory"} parametrized homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+homotopy+theory"} global homotopy theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie calculus
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            are constructed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} indexed
            over an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
            or of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
          %p#AtomicOrbital
            An important ingredient of this program is the concept of an
            %em
              atomic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbital+%24%5Cinfty%24-category"}
                orbital
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            which is defined in terms of two important properties of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong> Orbital
                \: Fiber products of representable presheaves are finite disjoint unions of representable presheaves, a restatement of the fact that the category of finite
                = succeed "-sets" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "double+coset#MackeyFormula"} Mackey decomposition
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
            %li
              %p
                %strong> Atomic
                \: The triviality of retracts (that is every retraction is an equivalence).
          %p
            Examples of such
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 1)
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+categories"} orbit categories
                of finite groups;
            %li
              %p
                more generally, orbit categories of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+groups"} profinite groups
                (where the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizers"} stabilizers
                are required to be
                = succeed ");" do
